{
  "about": "MM3D (USA rev 1) draws its button prompts as 3DS art; each cell below, in the texture's own pixels [x0, y0, x1, y1], is drawn as port-assets' Xbox pad glyph for the pad button the app binds there (A/B/X/Y by name, L/R the triggers, ZL/ZR the bumpers, START the menu button, the circle pad the left stick, the power button's cell (icon 9, which no message uses) View, for the text's map prompts; the text sheet's four item-button cells, X, Y, I and II, name where our item slots start: Y, B, RB and the D-pad). Boxes are placed on Henriko's 4K pack's art, so some sit on fractions of a pixel. inlay: the prompt sits on the art, which is filled in under the glyph. badge: the glyph is drawn over the art: over the pack's own button where it covers it, or on a touch button the pad reaches (ZL is View). chord: [held, pressed] in one cell, for the touch slots Project Restoration puts on ZR with X and Y. A texture in a GAR archive is <archive>.gar/<file>. {language} in a path stands for each of languages: the pack has English and Spanish sheets, with the prompts in the same cells, and no French ones. key: in the text's prompt sheet, the app's key bindings (`z3d --keys` lines, \"<table> <name>\") for that prompt, which the install draws as key caps in the sheet's keyboard image; a cell of several keys shows them in one cap.",
